codex
I found the toolchain failure’s concrete cause: the container’s PID namespace is not matched by its `/proc` mount, so Lean asks for `/proc/<namespace-pid>/exe` and receives `ENOENT`. A narrowly scoped preload shim that retries only that missing path as `/proc/self/exe` restores the pinned Lean 4.22 binary; the generated project’s clean build is now progressing under that correction.
